  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 8 is a split-delivery race: merge the two b blocks into the first c, kite it up the extreme left edge while two hunters fuse and the 8 is processed into the second c, then send that second c along the top edge to the far-right 9 socket. Clicking within attraction range of both c pieces merges them back into an 8. Level 9 revealed that ACTION7 is a true one-step undo, two 6 blocks merge into f, four hunters must apparently satisfy an additional d-shaped requirement, and final-level reset performs a full-game reset rather than restarting the current level.",
  "narrative": "The 132-action verified prefix reached Level 7 twice. I solved Level 8 live with a 13-action continuation and replayed that continuation successfully in a separately created environment after its own full prefix, reaching levels_completed=8 both times. I did not have enough budget left to run the required reproduce() gate on all 145 actions, so reproduction_verified is intentionally false. On Level 9 I produced and socketed c and f, discovered the still-unsatisfied d-shaped hunter-fusion requirement and ACTION7 undo, then stopped when the final-level environment entered GAME_OVER after repeated rewind experiments.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The Level 4 hunter advances about four pixels per axis toward the active/highest fruit; long axis-aligned 8-pixel fruit hops create separation, while diagonal hops often do not.",
    "A hunter collision may be rendered as partial occlusion for one frame; the fruit can survive if moved continuously, but an unmoved fruit is downgraded on the following action.",
    "Two 7-colored hunters can collide and fuse into an e-colored composite thief. The e sprite can remain largely hidden under a fruit and then repeatedly downgrade it on later actions.",
    "In Level 5 the resource meter is nearly exact: the verified line reaches the final target with only the last few meter cells remaining; avoid extra failed clicks.",
    "Level 6 collision resolution can be deferred: the verified tail reaches the win after a far failed click following the final c/hunter positioning.",
    "Level 7 needs two hops for the right b, via (48,24) then (44,22); clicking (44,22) directly from its spawn is outside pull range and wastes the critical timing window.",
    "Level 8: after the two b fruits merge into one c and the 8 is processed into the other c, never click a point within pull radius of both c fruits or they merge back into an 8.",
    "The Level 8 winning continuation is (10,42), (3,42), (3,35), (3,28), (3,21), (18,22), (18,16), (24,11), (31,12), (38,12), (45,12), (52,14), (56,19).",
